expected.stdout is the compile-time `--dump-mono-specs` output (main prints
nothing at runtime). The tree-walking interpreter has no monomorphization pass,
so `tur --interpret` produces no mono-spec lines and cannot match. run.sh
captures the dump via the single-process `tur run` path (requires.interp); this
marker tells run-turi.sh to skip the pure-interpret run rather than diff empty
stdout against the mono-spec assertion. The arity-mismatch bug this fixture
exercised (turi-interp-forall-dict-wide-consumer-arity) is fixed independently;
the sibling -clone and -forward fixtures assert real runtime output and pass
under --interpret.
